.TH mount 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
mount \- mount a filesystem, or show what is mounted
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mount
.br
.B mount
[\fB\-t\fI type\fR] \fIdevice\fR \fIdirectory\fR
.br
.B mount \-a
.SH DESCRIPTION
With no arguments,
.B mount
prints what is currently mounted, from
.BR /etc/mtab .
.PP
Given a
.I device
and a
.IR directory ,
it attaches that filesystem there.  Whatever was in the directory before
is hidden until it is unmounted, not lost.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a
Mount everything listed in
.B /etc/fstab
that is not already mounted.
.TP
.BI \-t " type"
The filesystem type.  FUZIX has one,
.BR fuzix ,
so this is rarely needed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/fstab
What should be mounted, and where.
.TP
.B /etc/mtab
What is mounted now.
.B mount
writes this; if it goes missing the list is lost, not the mounts.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# mount
# mount /dev/hda3 /mnt
# mount -a
.fi
.SH NOTES
The FAT partition of the card is not mounted and cannot be:
.BR fat (1)
reads it from outside the filesystem.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR umount (1),
.BR remount (1),
.BR df (1),
.BR fsck (1),
.BR fat (1)
